// Animals and people as bodies, fighters and herds (old AnimalFactory, AnimalType and the herd
// behaviours). Loaded once by Content; ContentTests checks every name in here resolves.
//
// species: every Species has one row.
//   body, weightKg, fatPct, musclePct: the body plan and its average build (members vary around it).
//   role: how it meets a threat. isSmall: small game, which runs where a big one of its role would not.
//   attackDamage, attackType: its unarmed attack. threat, boldness, aggression, cohesion: the morale
//   numbers combat runs on. moveAllowanceM: metres covered in one combat action at full Moving.
//   temperament: what makes its herd come at a target (a name in temperaments).
//   behavior: how its herd lives (old HerdBehaviorType; Carrion is the folded scavenger flock). diet: what its herd grazes (a name in diets).
//   Humans, rabbits and foxes never form herds of their own; theirs are the old defaults, Prey and Carnivore.
// temperaments: base, a bonus per member, hunger (hungryAt, starvingAt, hungerBonus), defending a kill
//   or den (defendBonus), and a ceiling (cap). Cap 0 never starts a fight.
// diets: what each Diet takes off a tile's forage, in order (old AnimalDietExtensions.GetConsumedResources).
// sightings: how watchful a stalked animal is, by what its herd is doing; one is picked at random
//   (old HuntingSightings' DetectionModifier values, pool by pool, in their order).
